---
/**
 * Shipping Policy.
 *
 * WHY A SERVICE STUDIO HAS ONE AT ALL. Nothing here is shipped, and a page
 * called "Shipping Policy" on a video production site looks like a template
 * left in by mistake. It is here because Indian payment gateways — Razorpay,
 * PayU, Cashfree — require a reachable shipping policy before they will
 * activate an account, and Rajesh asked for it by name.
 *
 * So it says the true thing rather than inventing couriers and dispatch
 * windows: this is a service, delivery is digital, and here is exactly how and
 * when files arrive. That satisfies the requirement honestly, and it is
 * genuinely useful to a client who wants to know how they will receive a
 * multi-camera day's footage.
 */
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business.ts';
---

<Legal
  title="Shipping & Delivery Policy | Beyond Pixel Studio"
  h1="Shipping & Delivery Policy"
  description="How Beyond Pixel Studio delivers finished films, photographs and raw footage — digitally, and by physical media where a job needs it."
  updated="2026-08-31"
>
  <p>
    <strong>{business.name}</strong> provides services, not physical products.
    There is nothing to ship in the ordinary sense: no goods are dispatched, no
    courier is used for a normal job, and there are no shipping charges.
  </p>
  <p>
    What we do deliver is files. This page explains how they reach you and when.
  </p>

  <h2>How work is delivered</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>What</th><th>How it reaches you</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Finished films, edits and photographs</td>
        <td>A download link, or a shared cloud folder, sent to the email address on your quote</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Live streams</td>
        <td>Streamed to your own channel during the event; a recording follows by link afterwards where the quote includes one</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Raw footage from a multi-camera day</td>
        <td>By transfer link, or copied to a drive — agreed at the quote stage, because the volume decides which is practical</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Physical media, where a job needs it</td>
        <td>Handed over in person in Bhubaneswar, or couriered at cost where agreed in writing</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When</h2>
  <p>
    Delivery timelines are stated in your quote, because they depend on the job:
    a single-camera interview and a multi-day event with several language
    versions are not the same piece of work. Where a deadline matters, say so in
    the first message and we will tell you plainly whether it is achievable
    before you book.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a delivery date has been agreed and something puts it at risk, you
    will hear it from us before the date, not after it.
  </p>

  <h2>Delivery charges</h2>
  <p>
    Digital delivery is included in every quote and costs nothing extra.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where you ask for physical media — a hard drive, a pen drive, printed
    photographs — the cost of the media and of any courier is itemised in the
    quote as a separate line, or agreed in writing before it is sent. We do not
    add delivery charges that were not quoted.
  </p>

  <h2>If something does not arrive</h2>
  <p>
    Download links can expire, land in spam, or be blocked by a corporate mail
    filter. If a delivery has not reached you, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or message{' '}
    <a href={business.phone.href}>{business.phone.display}</a> and we will send
    it again by another route. We keep delivered work on our own storage for a
    reasonable period after handover for exactly this reason.
  </p>

  <h2>Data protection</h2>
  <p>
    Delivering this work means holding your material — footage of your event,
    your staff, your premises, your customers — so how it is stored matters as
    much as how it is sent.
  </p>

  <h3>What we hold, and for how long</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Raw footage and project files</strong> stay on our own storage
      after delivery, so a lost download or a corrupted drive can be recovered
      rather than reshot. They are not kept indefinitely — tell us to delete
      them once you have your files and we will.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Delivered files</strong> are kept for a reasonable period after
      handover, for the same reason.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your contact details</strong> are covered by the
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>, which sets out exactly what
      is collected and where it goes.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Who can see it</h3>
  <p>
    Only the crew working on your job. Footage is not shared with other clients,
    not sold, and not passed to anyone outside {business.name}. Where a job
    needs an outside specialist, you are told before the shoot rather than
    after.
  </p>

  <h3>Transfer links</h3>
  <p>
    Download links are unlisted and sent to the address on your quote. They are
    not indexed and not published anywhere. Anyone holding the link can open it,
    so treat it as you would a password: if a link reaches the wrong person,
    tell us and we will revoke it and issue a new one.
  </p>

  <h3>People filmed at your event</h3>
  <p>
    At a public event, obtaining consent from those attending is the organiser's
    responsibility, not ours — you know who is in the room and what they agreed
    to. Where someone asks us directly not to be filmed, we will respect it on
    the day. If a person needs to be removed from delivered footage afterwards,
    tell us and we will do it where it is technically possible.
  </p>

  <h3>Confidential jobs</h3>
  <p>
    Some work should never appear in a portfolio — an internal briefing, an
    unreleased product, a site under NDA. Say so before the shoot and it is
    written into the quote as excluded, and it will not be shown on this site or
    on our social channels. We would rather be told early than take it down
    later.
  </p>

  <h3>Security, stated plainly</h3>
  <p>
    Files are held on access-controlled storage and transferred over encrypted
    connections. No storage or transfer method is completely secure, and we will
    not claim otherwise. If something goes wrong that affects your material, you
    will hear it from us.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we work</h2>
  <p>
    Shoots are carried out in {business.areaServed.join(', ')} and across
    {business.areaServedBroad}, with travel elsewhere itemised in the quote. AI
    video production is delivered nationwide. Digital delivery has no
    geographic limit.
  </p>
</Legal>
